9. Complete CWG Algorithm

Algorithm CWG (Environment E, maturity L, technology T, automation state A)

1. Constraint Extraction:
      Discretise environmental variables, run AC‑3 to obtain active constraints, generate ranked requirements R.
2. Functional Decomposition:
      Decompose each r\in R to atomic functions F_{\text{init}}. Construct DAG G_F; collapse SCCs.
3. Iterative Allocation and Coordination:
      Repeat until F stabilises:
   · Traverse functions in reverse topological order.
   · For each f, compute required capability vector \underline{\lambda}_f.
   · Compute U(a,f) for all agent types, assign \alpha^*(f)=\arg\max U(a,f).
   · If \alpha^*(f) is automated, generate supervision functions (bounded recursion, Lemma 2).
   · Update F and G_F.
4. Profession Generation:
   · Cluster functions into candidate professions based on competency and responsibility.
   · Compute fixed‑anchor normalised scores G(p); apply lexicographic filter (retain human oversight for f with \mathrm{crit}(f)>\theta_{\text{crit}}).
   · Determine r_{\min} via beta‑factor equation.
   · Run greedy set multi‑cover to obtain P.
5. Dependency Graph and Criticality:
   · Build profession DAG G_P.
   · Compute unconstrained critical path and resource bottleneck penalties to assign criticality scores.
   · For each critical function, verify k-resilience with topological diversity and beta‑factor constraint; add backup professions if needed, re‑running set cover locally.
6. Dynamic Relaxation and DNA Loop:
   · Between discovery jumps, apply \Phi_{\text{relax}} (contraction step) to converge to a stable configuration.
   · The outer GA loop optimises efficiency DNA parameters while keeping safety thresholds fixed.
   · Evaluate fitness by comparing generated profession set to lunar benchmark and satisfaction of resilience criteria.
7. Return profession ecosystem P, dependency graph G_P, criticality annotations.

Complexity.
All steps are polynomial or solved with guaranteed‑ratio heuristics, except the outer GA whose convergence is asymptotic but practically bounded. For |F|\approx 500, the entire pipeline runs in seconds on modern hardware.

