K.2 Causal Sensitivity Metric

For a perturbation \delta E (e.g., adding a large ice deposit), we rerun CWG to get P'. The sensitivity is

S(E,\delta) = \frac{d(P(E), P(E+\delta))}{\|\delta\|},

using the wGED metric. A non‑zero value demonstrates environment‑driven variation, not a fixed output.

